},{"id":"401892638000000900","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Giveaway by Tyson Foerster","type":{"id":"1402","text":"Giveaway","abbreviation":"giveaway"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:42"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"15"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4697406","displayName":"Tyson Foerster","shortName":"T. Foerster"},"type":"giver"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1845","fullName":"Xfinity Mobile Arena","address":{"city":"Philadelphia","state":"PA","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1845.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17889,"officials":[{"fullName":"Kyle Rehman","displayName":"Kyle Rehman","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Libor Suchanek","displayName":"Libor Suchanek","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Julien Fournier","displayName":"Julien Fournier","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Morgan MacPhee","displayName":"Morgan MacPhee","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Wild beat Flyers 4-2 after referee deflection leads to game-winning goal","description":"— Matt Boldy had a goal and an assist, and Joel Eriksson Ek scored what proved to be the winner after a Flyers clearing attempt hit a referee as the Minnesota Wild beat the Philadelphia Flyers 4-2 on Tuesday night.","story":"PHILADELPHIA -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565233/matt-boldy\">Matt Boldy</a> had a goal and an assist, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3904091/joel-eriksson-ek\">Joel Eriksson Ek</a> scored what proved to be the winner after a Flyers clearing attempt hit a referee as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/min/minnesota-wild\">Minnesota Wild</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/phi/philadelphia-flyers\">Philadelphia Flyers</a> 4-2 on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              The Wild scored two goals in 31 seconds in the first period. Boldy took a pass from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4320548/quinn-hughes\">Quinn Hughes</a> and snapped it from the high slot past Flyers goalie <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3942459/dan-vladar\">Dan Vladar</a> to open the scoring.\n\n\r\n              On the next shift, a pass from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2563026/blake-coleman\">Blake Coleman</a> hit off <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5291941/porter-martone\">Porter Martone</a>'s skate and caromed right to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042048/michael-mccarron\">Michael McCarron</a>, who wristed it past Vladar to make it 2-0. \n\n\r\n              The Flyers were unhappy with referee Kyle Rehman on the opening shift of the second period. A clearing pass from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697387/jamie-drysdale\">Jamie Drysdale</a> hit Rehman and created a 2-on-1 for Minnesota. Boldy fed a pass to Erikisson-Ek for a wrister that beat Vladar to extend the lead to 3-0.\n\n\r\n              Philadelphia's <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565230/trevor-zegras\">Trevor Zegras</a> shouted at Rehman and was immediately assessed a 10-minute misconduct. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874737/jesper-wallstedt\">Jesper Wallstedt</a> made 23 saves for the Wild, who extended their point streak to six games (5-0-1) and have won five straight on the road. \n\n\r\n              Philadelphia closed to within 3-2 on a goal by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697406/tyson-foerster\">Tyson Foerster</a> and a power-play goal by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5173105/denver-barkey\">Denver Barkey</a>, but the Wild iced the game when <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080172/danila-yurov\">Danila Yurov</a> scored an empty-net goal. \n\n\r\n              The line of <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3942335/kirill-kaprizov\">Kirill Kaprizov</a>, Eriksson Ek, and Boldy have now gone 17 games to start the season without being on the ice for a goal against. \n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Wild: Returns home to host San Jose on Friday.\n\n\r\n              Flyers: Begin a five-game road trip in New York against the Rangers on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-04T03:05:48Z"}}